Rejected at Step 0. The proposed family fails **H — hardness**.

[Theorems 1–2](https://arxiv.org/html/1910.13133v5#S2) explicitly construct the generator matrix through direct concatenation of the incidence matrix, identity matrix, and all-one column. Sections 3’s orbit-matrix variants are equally constructive. Verification is cheap, but so is finding the witness.

[Section 4](https://arxiv.org/html/1910.13133v5#S4) provides a finite catalog of 178 \(M_{11}\)-invariant designs, not an unlimited scalable hard regime. The paper states no hardness theorem that would support repurposing minimum distance or automorphism computation.

The detailed rejection is recorded in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1910.13133/REJECTED.md). I intentionally did not create a generator, fabricated gate results, or run the hardening loop.
